[42.13386, "o", "\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 18 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Let me do a quick smoke test to confirm package installation works:\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 19 tool call(s) so far\r\nPip is fully restored and working. Here's what happened and what I did:\r\n\r\n**Problem:** The `pip` package's source code (`pip/` directory and all its subpackages) had been removed from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/`, leaving only the metadata directory (`pip-24.3.1.dist-info`). This caused `pip3` and `python3 -m pip` to fail with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'`.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Extracted the bundled pip wheel (`pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl`) from Python's `ensurepip` module directly into site-packages. This restored the full pip package including all its vendored dependencies.\r\n\r\n**Verification:** `pip3 --version` and `python3 -m pip --version` both report `pip 24.3.1"]
[42.133864, "o", "`, and a dry-run install of `requests` succeeds.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=19 surface=48cd0ade3676\r\n"]
